/*
:name: spec_types_cast_range_tuple
:type: comptime
:verifier_pass: 3
:verifier_fail: 0
*/
// SPEC docs 04-variables "Basic types" / "Range": "Range type cast from integers use the same one-hot encoding.
// It is not possible to type cast from tuple to range, but it is possible from range to tuple." and the examples
// "cassert(range(0ub01_1100) == 2..=4)", "cassert((1,2,3) == tuple(1..=3))",
// "cassert(tuple(0..=10 step  2) == ( 0,2,4,6,8,10))".
// NOTE: the lowercase `range`/`tuple` cast spelling is an open question (qa.md section 1 capitalizes every
// built-in type; Q15 lists no Range type).
cassert(range(0ub01_1100) == 2..=4)
cassert((1,2,3) == tuple(1..=3))
cassert(tuple(0..=10 step 2) == (0,2,4,6,8,10))
